{"role":"user","content":"You need to read an Excel file and answer a question about its contents.\n\nFile path: D:\\GoatCode-ts\\gaia\\data\\4d51c4bf-4b0e-4f3d-897b-3f6687a7d9f2.xlsx\n\nUse Python with openpyxl to read the file. First, install openpyxl if needed with `pip install openpyxl`. Then read the workbook and print all rows from the active sheet.\n\nThe data contains a list of clients for a retractable awning company. Each client ordered an awning for the back of their house. The company makes different designs depending on whether the awning is made to block sunrises or sunsets.\n\nKey facts:\n- Houses with odd-numbered street addresses face east\n- Houses with even-numbered street addresses face west\n- The awning is for the BACK of the house\n- We need to count how many clients will receive the SUNSET awning design\n\nThink step by step:\n1. Read all the data from the spreadsheet\n2. For each client, determine which direction their house faces based on their street address number (odd = east, even = west)\n3. Determine which direction the back of the house faces (opposite of the front)\n4. In the northern hemisphere (typical for this kind of question), the sun rises in the east and sets in the west\n5. So if the back of the house faces east, it blocks sunrise; if it faces west, it blocks sunset\n6. Count clients whose back faces west (sunset awning)\n\nReturn the final count as a number."}
